<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish July s/a trade surplus 727.6 mln punts - CSO.</title>
<headline>Irish July s/a trade surplus 727.6 mln punts - CSO.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's seasonally-adjusted trade surplus widened to 727.6 million punts in July from 639.7 million in June, Central Statistics Office (CSO) figures showed on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The CSO said provisional figures for August show imports trade at 1,490 million punts and exports are estimated at 1,930 million punts, giving a trade surplus of 440 million.</p>
<p>			   Imports	Exports	     Gap</p>
<p> July 1996	     1,788.7	2,516.3	     727.6</p>
<p> June 1996	     1,864.9	2,504.6	     639.7</p>
<p> July 1995	     1,647.9	2,236.3	     588.4</p>
<p>		   (Figures in millions of punts)</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom 353 1 660 3377</p>
